Why the plugin's header and not openxla/xla HEAD
------------------------------------------------
`PJRT_Api` is a table of function pointers whose size follows the API version: an
older plugin hands back a *shorter* table. Reading past its end would yield
garbage pointers, hence the explicit refusal when
`pjrt_api_version.minor_version < min_api_minor` (see `src/pjrt/client.zig`).

Reasoning the other way — "newer header than plugin, therefore lower
`min_api_minor`" — does not hold: the entries added after 0.81 are holes the plugin
will never fill. The header must therefore track the plugin, not the other way
round, and `client.zig` carries a `comptime` check that fails if the two diverge.

Updating
--------
    PJRT_VERSION=<exact> ./scripts/package_pjrt_releases.sh
then replace this file with the wheel's header and update the two values above
as well as `min_api_minor`.